<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n98242" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύμβᾰμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμβαίνω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111
				</span></i>
			) <i>chance, casualty</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Vit.Auct.</u>
				21
			</span></i> (but as a parody on signf. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				7.58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Palaeph.
				2(5)
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>misfortune</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Goth.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i> (dub. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aed.</u>
				4.3
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Stoic
			Philos., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηγόρημα</span>
			, <i>complete predicate</i>, such as an intrans. Verb, e.g.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σωκράτης περιπατεῖ</span>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρασύμβαμα, παρακατηγόρημα</span>,
			e.g. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σωκράτει μεταμέλει</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.59
			</span></i>.</div>
